@using BlazingStory.Components
@using Microsoft.FluentUI.AspNetCore.Components
@using Norse.DesignSystem.Stories
@using Norse.Infrastructure.Components.Theme.FluentUI
@*
    Spike note (Task 4, 2026-08-22): this indirection is load-bearing, not incidental. Putting
    @rendermode directly on <BlazingStoryApp> makes ASP.NET Core treat it as the interactive-server
    render-mode boundary, which tries to JSON-serialize its parameters (Assemblies: IEnumerable
    <Assembly>) into the boundary marker — Assembly/TypeInfo is not JSON-serializable, and the
    request 500s (System.NotSupportedException). A parameterless wrapper carries the boundary
    instead; NorseFluentDesignTheme, FluentProviders, and BlazingStoryApp are all plain children
    that inherit interactivity for free, no serialization involved. See
    ../Glitnir/docs/Platform/specs/2026-08-22-stories-blazor-server-mcp-design.md.
*@
<NorseFluentDesignTheme/>
<FluentProviders/>
<BlazingStoryApp Assemblies="[typeof(AssemblyMarker).Assembly]"/>
